@startuml dataflow_example_parallel
' Worked example: the parallel path, one variable on a 4x4 grid in two
' chunks, compared with the serial run of the same call without max_obs.
' Every number here is from actual runs.
' Grids: rows x0 (= dim_split), columns x1, index space.
' Render: plantuml docs/dataflow_example_parallel.puml

title Example 6 -- the parallel path: two chunks that reproduce the serial data (experimental)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "call" {
  :if ~__name~__ == "~__main~__":
      GenerateData(num_obs=10, num_dims=2, ratio_dims=1,
                   density=10/16, seed=12345, <b>max_obs=5</b>)
      .generate(netcdf_filepath=".../netCDF/ds.nc",
                parquet_filepath=".../parquet/ddf",
                parquet_tmp=".../parquet/tmp");
  note right
    Workers start with the spawn method, which
    re-imports the calling script: without the
    ~__main~__ guard each worker would start the
    run again.
  end note
}

partition "validate and configure" {
  :shape = [4, 4], 16 sites, <b>dim_split = 0</b>;

  :<b>_multiprocessing_setup</b>
  NTASKS = ceil(10 / 5) = 2
  the split axis has 4 strata -> block sizes 2, 2
  div_points = 0, 2, 4;
  note right
    printed:
    "Parallel generation: 2 tasks, 5 obs per task
      Dataset split along dimension 0
      Block sizes along it: [2, 2]"
    NTASKS cannot exceed the length of the split axis
    (here 4): see diagnostic S6.
  end note
}

partition "parallel setup (main process)" {
  :<b>ChunkUtils.get_observations_per_chunk</b>
  apportion 10 over the 2 blocks -> 5, 5
  printed: "Observations per chunk: [5, 5] (total 10).";

  :one argument dict per chunk, plain values only
  ProcessPoolExecutor(spawn, max_workers = min(2, cpu_count));
}

partition "each worker: generate_chunk(chunk_id, ...)" {
  :<b>coordinates</b>: drawn over the GLOBAL shape with the
  same streams as serial, then the split axis is sliced
    x0 (global) = 0.1809, 0.3500 | 0.5382, 0.6837
    chunk 0 gets the first two, chunk 1 the last two
    x1 = 0.2162, 0.7887, 0.9100, 0.9353 in both;

  :<b>LHS stage</b>, recomputed in full by EVERY worker
  stream(12345, LHS), n_s = 4 -> sites (0,2), (1,0), (2,1), (3,3)
  fill per stratum = 1, 1, 2, 2 (the same apportionment);
  note right
    after the LHS stage, global grid
    (L = LHS site, - - = chunk boundary)
            x1=0 x1=1 x1=2 x1=3
      x0=0   .    .    L    .      chunk 0
      x0=1   L    .    .    .
      - - - - - - - - - - - - -
      x0=2   .    L    .    .      chunk 1
      x0=3   .    .    .    L
    4 points: each worker repeats this for a few
    hundred bytes rather than receive it.
  end note

  :<b>its own strata only</b>
  chunk 0: strata 0, 1 with stream(12345, STRATUM, 0) and (.., 1)
  chunk 1: strata 2, 3 with stream(12345, STRATUM, 2) and (.., 3)
  global indices, then the split axis is rebased:
  local x0 = x0 - div_points[chunk_id];
  note right
    chunk 0 record, 2x4      chunk 1 record, 2x4
    (f = fill site)          (local x0 0, 1 = global 2, 3)
            x1=0 x1=1 x1=2 x1=3          x1=0 x1=1 x1=2 x1=3
      x0=0   f    .    L    .      x0=2   f    L    .    f
      x0=1   L    f    .    .      x0=3   .    f    f    L
    No stream tuple contains a chunk id, so each stratum
    is the same draw it is in the serial run.
  end note

  :write <b>netCDF/ds_0.nc</b> / <b>ds_1.nc</b>
  (squeeze_constant_dims=False: chunks keep every dim)
  and <b>parquet/tmp/chunk_0000.parquet</b> / <b>chunk_0001.parquet</b>,
  rows in x0 order;
}

partition "consolidation (main process)" {
  :<b>_consolidate_parquet_files</b>
  dd.read_parquet(tmp/chunk_*.parquet).repartition("300MB")
  -> parquet/ddf_0.parquet, then the tmp directory is removed;

  :merge_nc=False (the default): the two chunk files stay
  <b>_describe</b> opens them together with open_mfdataset
  along x0 and prints the description;
  note right
    record, both chunks concatenated along x0
             x1=0    x1=1    x1=2    x1=3
      x0=0   0.320     .     0.550     .
      x0=1   0.742   0.023     .       .
      x0=2   0.868   0.134     .     0.653
      x0=3     .     0.412   0.538   0.761
    Identical to the serial record, value for value.
  end note
}

:return (None, None) -- the data exist only on disk;

partition "disk, parallel against serial" {
  :parallel                          serial
  netCDF/ds_0.nc         10508 B    netCDF/ds.nc         10500 B
  netCDF/ds_1.nc         10508 B
  parquet/ddf_0.parquet   3388 B    parquet/ddf_0.parquet 3407 B
  parquet/_metadata       2891 B    parquet/_metadata     2891 B;
  note right
    Same 10 rows with the same x0, x1, record values in
    both parquet outputs. The only column that differs is
    dask's ~__null_dask_index~__: 0..9 in serial, restarting
    in each chunk in parallel (0..3, then 0..5).
  end note
}

stop

@enduml
